1
00:00:12,429 --> 00:00:13,972
‎Feel that chill!

2
00:00:14,055 --> 00:00:15,682
‎Now, that is how autumn feels.

3
00:00:17,475 --> 00:00:19,978
‎I love these moments
‎where you really feel the season.

4
00:00:20,061 --> 00:00:21,938
‎You say that a lot.

5
00:00:22,022 --> 00:00:25,191
{\an8}‎I love summer events
‎with their summer vibes,

6
00:00:25,275 --> 00:00:28,319
{\an8}‎and I love that cool-but-still-muggy
‎feeling you get

7
00:00:28,403 --> 00:00:31,072
{\an8}‎when you go for a walk in summer at night...

8
00:00:31,781 --> 00:00:33,033
‎But moments like these,

9
00:00:33,116 --> 00:00:36,202
‎when it gets cool
‎and you feel the seasonal change,

10
00:00:36,286 --> 00:00:39,039
‎these are the moments
‎that get me the most excited.

11
00:00:39,122 --> 00:00:41,207
{\an8}‎I think I get you.

12
00:00:41,291 --> 00:00:44,127
‎It's kind of like when you do
‎a long slog of summer workouts,

13
00:00:44,210 --> 00:00:47,005
‎and then you feel like,
‎"Whoa, am I stronger now?"

14
00:00:47,088 --> 00:00:51,217
‎Maybe it's that sensation
‎still in my mind. Do you think?

15
00:00:51,301 --> 00:00:53,595
‎I take it back. I don't get you at all.

16
00:00:53,678 --> 00:00:54,929
‎Why not?

17
00:01:02,020 --> 00:01:03,021
‎Autumn.

18
00:01:04,230 --> 00:01:05,940
‎When's your birthday, Amamiya?

19
00:01:06,566 --> 00:01:08,485
‎Will you do something for me?

20
00:01:08,568 --> 00:01:10,820
‎No, don't expect anything special...

21
00:01:11,529 --> 00:01:13,114
{\an8}<i>‎It's September 29th.</i>

22
00:01:14,199 --> 00:01:15,200
{\an8}<i>‎It's coming up.</i>

23
00:01:15,784 --> 00:01:18,119
<i>‎His birthday's coming up soon.</i>

24
00:01:18,203 --> 00:01:19,204
<i>‎But...</i>

25
00:01:19,788 --> 00:01:20,789
‎All right.

26
00:01:21,790 --> 00:01:23,708
{\an8}‎I'll stay away from Amamiya.

27
00:01:24,584 --> 00:01:27,462
<i>‎I said that so assertively, but...</i>

28
00:01:28,296 --> 00:01:30,924
<i>‎How much distance do I need to keep?</i>

29
00:01:31,007 --> 00:01:33,176
<i>‎We never actually drew the line.</i>

30
00:01:33,259 --> 00:01:35,970
<i>‎Can I give him a birthday present?
‎No, that's got to be off-limits.</i>

31
00:01:36,054 --> 00:01:37,055
<i>‎Happy birthday!</i>

32
00:01:37,889 --> 00:01:40,225
<i>‎What about in a nonserious sort of way?</i>

33
00:01:40,308 --> 00:01:44,479
<i>‎Still, he's given me so much
‎that I'd like to return the favor.</i>

34
00:01:45,855 --> 00:01:50,735
<i>‎He wasn't at school over the weekend,
‎so I'm a little worried about him.</i>

35
00:01:51,361 --> 00:01:53,613
<i>‎I want to ask him if he's okay,</i>

36
00:01:54,447 --> 00:01:57,075
<i>‎but I'm not in the position to do that.</i>

37
00:02:01,329 --> 00:02:02,330
‎GRADE 2 CLASS 2

38
00:02:02,413 --> 00:02:03,706
‎What? Seriously?

39
00:02:04,582 --> 00:02:07,001
‎You really broke up with Kuriki?

40
00:03:39,552 --> 00:03:43,932
‎EPISODE 22
‎TURNING POINTS

41
00:03:44,599 --> 00:03:47,143
‎A FEW DAYS EARLIER

42
00:03:47,769 --> 00:03:49,395
<i>‎Are you feeling okay?</i>

43
00:03:51,731 --> 00:03:54,150
<i>‎Thanks. I'm fine now.</i>

44
00:03:58,238 --> 00:04:00,323
‎I'M SORRY, MOMOKA
‎WE NEED TO TALK

45
00:04:00,406 --> 00:04:01,658
<i>‎Until now...</i>

46
00:04:02,617 --> 00:04:03,660
‎I want to break up.

47
00:04:04,911 --> 00:04:05,912
‎Okay.

48
00:04:07,038 --> 00:04:11,793
{\an8}<i>‎I've been pragmatic about things
‎because I thought it's what they wanted.</i>

49
00:04:11,876 --> 00:04:15,213
<i>‎It's just easier when others
‎are the ones making the decisions.</i>

50
00:04:16,381 --> 00:04:19,008
<i>‎If it's not my choice,</i>

51
00:04:19,092 --> 00:04:20,969
<i>‎it's not my failure.</i>

52
00:04:21,761 --> 00:04:23,179
<i>‎I'm the dumpee,</i>

53
00:04:23,846 --> 00:04:25,640
<i>‎so I'm not the one inflicting the pain.</i>

54
00:04:26,516 --> 00:04:28,559
<i>‎So long as I meet people's expectations,</i>

55
00:04:29,143 --> 00:04:31,688
<i>‎I'm not the perpetrator,
‎and I'm not the bad guy,</i>

56
00:04:32,355 --> 00:04:35,817
<i>‎I act like this
‎because I don't want to be responsible.</i>

57
00:04:36,901 --> 00:04:39,070
{\an8}‎I'M SORRY, MOMOKA
‎WE NEED TO TALK - READ

58
00:04:39,779 --> 00:04:44,367
<i>‎Who knew initiating a breakup
‎would feel so heavy?</i>

59
00:04:45,618 --> 00:04:47,912
‎You just got dumped,
‎but you're acting totally fine.

60
00:04:48,454 --> 00:04:50,373
‎Rude. I do feel hurt.

61
00:04:50,456 --> 00:04:51,666
‎ME BEFORE...

62
00:04:54,711 --> 00:04:56,921
<i>‎I was preoccupied with sensing the mood</i>

63
00:04:57,005 --> 00:05:00,550
<i>‎and doing what I thought
‎everyone else wanted.</i>

64
00:05:00,633 --> 00:05:03,553
<i>‎I'd stick my nose in
‎just to feel good about myself,</i>

65
00:05:03,636 --> 00:05:06,389
<i>‎then bask in the attention
‎whenever people looked toward me.</i>

66
00:05:06,889 --> 00:05:08,224
<i>‎"See? It's all right."</i>

67
00:05:08,808 --> 00:05:11,227
<i>‎"This is the right thing to do."
‎Or so I thought.</i>

68
00:05:12,854 --> 00:05:14,272
<i>‎But in reality...</i>

69
00:05:15,023 --> 00:05:16,274
‎You know what, Minato?

70
00:05:17,066 --> 00:05:19,777
‎You really don't have a sense of self.

71
00:05:20,862 --> 00:05:22,613
<i>‎I was a shell of a person,</i>

72
00:05:23,406 --> 00:05:25,867
<i>‎filling myself up with others.</i>

73
00:05:27,869 --> 00:05:28,870
<i>‎I'm...</i>

74
00:05:29,620 --> 00:05:30,913
<i>‎a mess.</i>

75
00:05:32,874 --> 00:05:34,625
‎I'M SORRY, MOMOKA
‎WE NEED TO TALK

76
00:05:34,709 --> 00:05:36,294
<i>‎He wants to "talk."</i>

77
00:05:36,919 --> 00:05:38,963
<i>‎As soon as he said it,</i>

78
00:05:39,714 --> 00:05:42,050
<i>‎I knew what he wanted to "talk" about.</i>

79
00:05:42,717 --> 00:05:46,763
<i>‎I've been more and more on edge
‎ever since we started dating.</i>

80
00:05:50,016 --> 00:05:52,268
<i>‎That's it. I'm done for today.</i>

81
00:05:53,436 --> 00:05:57,106
<i>‎It's not like he notices
‎how hard I try anyway.</i>

82
00:05:58,316 --> 00:06:02,361
<i>‎I used to try so hard for myself,
‎but now it's like I can't anymore.</i>

83
00:06:02,862 --> 00:06:05,323
<i>‎The lack of recognition
‎makes me feel insecure.</i>

84
00:06:06,282 --> 00:06:11,579
<i>‎I stuck to my guns because I didn't
‎want to become the kind of girl I hate,</i>

85
00:06:12,622 --> 00:06:17,293
<i>‎but now I feel like I'm becoming
‎somebody I don't want to be.</i>

86
00:06:19,420 --> 00:06:20,463
<i>‎I'm...</i>

87
00:06:21,089 --> 00:06:22,381
<i>‎sick of it all.</i>

88
00:06:35,728 --> 00:06:36,896
‎We should break up.

89
00:06:38,481 --> 00:06:40,858
<i>‎Yeah. I knew it.</i>

90
00:06:41,734 --> 00:06:44,904
‎Are you breaking up with me
‎so you can go after who you really like?

91
00:06:46,280 --> 00:06:47,281
‎No.

92
00:06:47,907 --> 00:06:49,242
‎That's not the reason.

93
00:06:50,618 --> 00:06:52,078
‎It's not you.

94
00:06:53,454 --> 00:06:55,039
‎It's me.

95
00:06:57,208 --> 00:07:00,795
‎I can't change it, even if we keep dating.

96
00:07:01,712 --> 00:07:04,090
‎I can't be who you want me to be.

97
00:07:06,217 --> 00:07:08,052
<i>‎I think I like her.</i>

98
00:07:08,719 --> 00:07:11,055
<i>‎I want her to be happy.</i>

99
00:07:12,265 --> 00:07:13,266
<i>‎But...</i>

100
00:07:13,891 --> 00:07:17,603
<i>‎I don't think I have to be
‎the one to make her happy.</i>

101
00:07:19,147 --> 00:07:21,274
<i>‎I don't want to "make" her happy.</i>

102
00:07:21,858 --> 00:07:23,317
<i>‎I want her to "be" happy.</i>

103
00:07:24,777 --> 00:07:25,945
‎I don't think

104
00:07:27,155 --> 00:07:28,489
‎what I feel is really love.

105
00:07:29,824 --> 00:07:30,825
‎I'm sorry.

106
00:07:35,496 --> 00:07:36,622
‎I...

107
00:07:37,290 --> 00:07:39,750
‎I already knew you felt like this.

108
00:07:39,834 --> 00:07:40,835
‎Stupid, stupid, stupid!

109
00:07:40,918 --> 00:07:45,089
‎I knew you never liked me.
‎I knew you felt obligated.

110
00:07:45,173 --> 00:07:46,966
‎I knew it all along.

111
00:07:47,049 --> 00:07:49,594
‎You don't know how hard it's been for me!

112
00:07:52,597 --> 00:07:53,598
‎I'm sorry.

113
00:07:54,223 --> 00:07:55,475
‎If only I'd said it sooner--

114
00:07:55,558 --> 00:07:57,977
‎Don't you dare say
‎you wish we'd never gone out.

115
00:08:00,146 --> 00:08:03,316
‎Don't reject it all like that.

116
00:08:06,903 --> 00:08:11,449
‎I would have preferred you telling me
‎you like someone else.

117
00:08:12,492 --> 00:08:14,952
‎But to say "It's not you, it's me,"

118
00:08:15,620 --> 00:08:18,623
‎to decide that all on your own
‎without consulting me first,

119
00:08:18,706 --> 00:08:22,752
‎that's like saying you don't think
‎I can help you with your problems.

120
00:08:23,336 --> 00:08:26,506
‎It's like you're saying I'm not someone
‎you want to open your heart up to.

121
00:08:28,591 --> 00:08:29,592
{\an8}‎Whatever.

122
00:08:30,426 --> 00:08:33,137
<i>‎I'm sick of worrying about all of this.</i>

123
00:08:34,388 --> 00:08:35,932
<i>‎Stay that way.</i>

124
00:08:36,474 --> 00:08:38,518
<i>‎Keep your heart locked up, for all I care.</i>

125
00:08:44,857 --> 00:08:45,942
‎BONK

126
00:08:47,527 --> 00:08:48,819
‎Fine. I get it.

127
00:08:49,946 --> 00:08:50,947
‎We're finished.

128
00:08:52,281 --> 00:08:53,574
‎You idiot.

129
00:09:03,501 --> 00:09:04,627
<i>‎It's over.</i>

130
00:09:06,462 --> 00:09:09,382
<i>‎It's over. It's over. It's finally over.</i>

131
00:09:10,299 --> 00:09:12,718
<i>‎I'd be lying if I said I wasn't sad,</i>

132
00:09:13,386 --> 00:09:17,974
<i>‎but I'm also a little relieved that
‎I don't have to worry so much anymore.</i>

133
00:09:18,849 --> 00:09:20,810
<i>‎Yeah. I'll be okay.</i>

134
00:09:21,310 --> 00:09:22,478
<i>‎I'm glad it's over.</i>

135
00:09:23,062 --> 00:09:24,230
<i>‎That's how I'll see it.</i>

136
00:09:27,775 --> 00:09:29,735
‎I'm going to delete all the photos.

137
00:09:36,325 --> 00:09:39,287
<i>‎We started dating over the summer break,</i>

138
00:09:39,370 --> 00:09:42,039
<i>‎so we caught up a lot
‎and got so many different photos.</i>

139
00:09:45,501 --> 00:09:47,378
<i>‎He really is quite handsome.</i>

140
00:09:47,461 --> 00:09:50,464
{\an8}<i>‎No. Do not be swayed, girl!</i>

141
00:09:52,925 --> 00:09:57,763
{\an8}<i>‎He remembered me saying
‎I wanted to watch this movie.</i>

142
00:09:58,556 --> 00:10:00,641
{\an8}<i>‎And how I wanted to go here.</i>

143
00:10:03,477 --> 00:10:07,898
<i>‎He even stayed up late with me
‎when I wanted to talk on the phone.</i>

144
00:10:08,774 --> 00:10:11,736
<i>‎We had so much fun together.</i>

145
00:10:13,362 --> 00:10:14,655
‎Minato.

146
00:10:15,489 --> 00:10:16,907
‎Do you even like me?

147
00:10:17,491 --> 00:10:18,951
{\an8}‎Yeah. I like you.

148
00:10:19,035 --> 00:10:20,077
{\an8}‎What do you like about me?

149
00:10:20,161 --> 00:10:23,831
{\an8}‎I like that you're confident
‎and feisty... and you're clever.

150
00:10:23,914 --> 00:10:27,418
{\an8}‎Aren't those sort of backhanded
‎compliments to give to a girl?

151
00:10:28,836 --> 00:10:30,296
‎But it's good to be cautious.

152
00:10:31,964 --> 00:10:35,551
<i>‎I always hated being treated like a doll.</i>

153
00:10:36,886 --> 00:10:38,721
<i>‎I hated being someone's accessory,</i>

154
00:10:39,430 --> 00:10:43,142
<i>‎and people coming up with a certain image
‎of me based on how I look.</i>

155
00:10:43,225 --> 00:10:44,560
‎I THINK YOU'D LIKE THIS, MOMOKA

156
00:10:44,644 --> 00:10:45,686
‎WOW, I DO! YAY!

157
00:10:45,770 --> 00:10:46,771
<i>‎But he...</i>

158
00:10:47,813 --> 00:10:49,357
<i>‎He saw me for who I am.</i>

159
00:10:49,982 --> 00:10:51,651
<i>‎He tried to get to know me.</i>

160
00:10:52,818 --> 00:10:54,195
<i>‎But still, after all that...</i>

161
00:10:55,988 --> 00:10:57,406
<i>‎he didn't choose me.</i>

162
00:10:59,659 --> 00:11:04,205
<i>‎Why am I only seeing all of the good
‎now that it's all over?</i>

163
00:11:05,122 --> 00:11:09,335
<i>‎Why couldn't I notice how kind
‎he was being while we were dating?</i>

164
00:11:10,711 --> 00:11:14,924
<i>‎Instead of focusing on what was lacking
‎and getting myself all worked up,</i>

165
00:11:15,591 --> 00:11:19,595
<i>‎I should have been thankful for all of the
‎attentive and kind things he did for me.</i>

166
00:11:19,678 --> 00:11:22,098
<i>‎If all you ever do is act
‎in your own self-interests,</i>

167
00:11:23,015 --> 00:11:25,101
‎you'll end up focusing on
‎all the parts where you're lacking.

168
00:11:26,227 --> 00:11:28,854
‎In the end, it'll only leave you unhappy.

169
00:11:31,690 --> 00:11:35,111
‎FLAILING

170
00:11:38,739 --> 00:11:39,782
‎No way.

171
00:11:39,865 --> 00:11:42,910
‎I thought they said Amamiya
‎is always the dumpee?

172
00:11:42,993 --> 00:11:44,370
‎Maybe he really was cheating?

173
00:11:44,453 --> 00:11:46,372
‎You know, with that girl from the stairs?

174
00:11:46,455 --> 00:11:47,873
‎What a scumbag.

175
00:11:49,375 --> 00:11:50,459
‎Momoka.

176
00:11:52,253 --> 00:11:53,921
‎Wakey wakey. Let's go home.

177
00:11:54,004 --> 00:11:55,381
‎Come on, cheer up.

178
00:11:55,464 --> 00:11:57,591
‎Wanna get something yummy on the way home?

179
00:11:57,675 --> 00:11:59,135
‎Today can be a cheat day.

180
00:11:59,218 --> 00:12:01,887
‎Come and vent. Let it all out.

181
00:12:03,931 --> 00:12:05,141
‎Thanks.

182
00:12:05,224 --> 00:12:06,642
‎BAM

183
00:12:08,269 --> 00:12:10,020
‎This isn't exactly what I expected.

184
00:12:10,104 --> 00:12:11,897
‎IMAGE - LET'S STRESS EAT
‎OUR SORROWS AWAY - GIGGLE GIGGLE

185
00:12:12,898 --> 00:12:13,899
‎You know what?

186
00:12:14,608 --> 00:12:18,279
‎I'm going to make sure I can love myself
‎more in my next relationship.

187
00:12:19,530 --> 00:12:21,740
‎I'll love who I am,

188
00:12:22,450 --> 00:12:26,412
‎and I'll find someone who loves me equally
‎as much so they only have eyes for me.

189
00:12:29,707 --> 00:12:33,127
‎If he feels distant at all,
‎I'll dump him right away.

190
00:12:33,919 --> 00:12:35,921
‎And if he dumps me,
‎I won't even be bothered,

191
00:12:36,005 --> 00:12:38,424
‎because I'll know
‎it just means he has no taste.

192
00:12:39,425 --> 00:12:42,428
‎That's the kind of girl I'm going to be.

193
00:12:45,681 --> 00:12:46,932
‎-Sounds great.
‎-Sounds great.

194
00:12:47,016 --> 00:12:48,017
‎YEAH!

195
00:12:48,100 --> 00:12:50,394
‎Good thinking! You go, girl!

196
00:12:51,479 --> 00:12:53,564
‎This is so spicy.

197
00:12:53,647 --> 00:12:56,567
‎But it tastes so good.

198
00:12:56,650 --> 00:12:57,860
‎You got this!

199
00:12:57,943 --> 00:12:58,944
‎BLAZING CHINESE GYOSHO

200
00:13:00,654 --> 00:13:03,365
<i>‎Amamiya and Momoka broke up.</i>

201
00:13:03,449 --> 00:13:04,450
‎GRADE 2 CLASS 2

202
00:13:04,533 --> 00:13:05,868
<i>‎It all happened so suddenly.</i>

203
00:13:06,827 --> 00:13:10,122
<i>‎I'd like to be happy,
‎given my position, but...</i>

204
00:13:11,165 --> 00:13:15,127
‎Dang, would you look at him?
‎Can hardly josh with him this time.

205
00:13:15,711 --> 00:13:18,380
‎He's been emotionally dead
‎ever since yesterday.

206
00:13:18,464 --> 00:13:20,758
‎Hino! Do something about this!

207
00:13:20,841 --> 00:13:23,093
‎I can't do anything about this.

208
00:13:24,261 --> 00:13:25,262
<i>‎Before...</i>

209
00:13:25,930 --> 00:13:31,227
‎I'm thankful they liked me,
‎even for a short time.

210
00:13:32,186 --> 00:13:35,940
<i>‎He seemed quite nonchalant
‎after a breakup.</i>

211
00:13:36,440 --> 00:13:39,109
<i>‎I thought that's just how he was, but...</i>

212
00:13:40,653 --> 00:13:42,363
‎PEEK

213
00:13:49,537 --> 00:13:52,373
‎Amamiya. Are you feeling better today?

214
00:13:53,791 --> 00:13:55,793
‎ZONKED

215
00:13:56,961 --> 00:13:58,921
{\an8}‎Yeah. I'm fine now.

216
00:13:59,713 --> 00:14:00,714
{\an8}‎Thanks.

217
00:14:02,049 --> 00:14:04,093
‎Yeah? That's good.

218
00:14:07,221 --> 00:14:08,597
‎Koyun!

219
00:14:08,681 --> 00:14:12,893
‎Hey! This is super hard!
‎He's like a completely different person.

220
00:14:12,977 --> 00:14:13,978
<i>‎We just broke up.</i>

221
00:14:14,562 --> 00:14:15,646
{\an8}‎Just like Midorikawa said.

222
00:14:15,729 --> 00:14:16,730
{\an8}‎CAN'T JOSH WITH HIM

223
00:14:17,356 --> 00:14:19,567
‎I want you to stay away from Minato.

224
00:14:20,484 --> 00:14:23,612
<i>‎I find it hard to believe
‎that Momoka would be the instigator.</i>

225
00:14:24,905 --> 00:14:26,198
<i>‎So was it Amamiya?</i>

226
00:14:27,408 --> 00:14:28,701
<i>‎If so...</i>

227
00:14:29,285 --> 00:14:31,871
‎Koyuki. Now's your chance.

228
00:14:31,954 --> 00:14:32,955
‎Tsukko!

229
00:14:33,038 --> 00:14:38,252
{\an8}‎Just think... Plug that hole in his heart
‎while he's feeling down now, and then...

230
00:14:38,335 --> 00:14:40,462
{\an8}‎Yes! Do that, Koyun.

231
00:14:47,011 --> 00:14:51,348
<i>‎Plugging the hole in his heart
‎might be the right thing to do</i>

232
00:14:51,432 --> 00:14:53,225
<i>‎if he really is heartbroken
‎over a breakup.</i>

233
00:14:55,311 --> 00:14:57,563
‎Did you hear? Koyuki dumped Igarashi.

234
00:14:57,646 --> 00:15:00,316
‎Really? Were they not doing so well?

235
00:15:01,400 --> 00:15:05,070
<i>‎But if he's feeling guilty,
‎or beating himself up over it,</i>

236
00:15:06,780 --> 00:15:10,576
<i>‎is there really anything
‎I can do to help him?</i>

237
00:15:12,786 --> 00:15:14,246
{\an8}‎Did you really break up with Kuriki?

238
00:15:15,414 --> 00:15:16,582
‎Yeah.

239
00:15:16,665 --> 00:15:19,835
‎Mind if I have a go next?

240
00:15:19,919 --> 00:15:22,254
‎Are you more a man of integrity?

241
00:15:22,338 --> 00:15:23,589
‎No, nothing like that.

242
00:15:24,590 --> 00:15:27,468
‎I'm not in any position
‎to tell people what to do.

243
00:15:27,551 --> 00:15:30,888
‎Well, knowing you, you'll have
‎yourself a new girlfriend in no time.

244
00:15:30,971 --> 00:15:31,972
‎AHAHA

245
00:15:38,604 --> 00:15:40,272
‎Azumi. Azumi!

246
00:15:42,191 --> 00:15:43,525
‎Akahoshi?

247
00:15:43,609 --> 00:15:44,944
‎How's Amamiya doing?

248
00:15:45,027 --> 00:15:48,030
‎Yeah. Still down in the dumps.

249
00:15:48,113 --> 00:15:49,114
‎The dumps, huh?

250
00:15:49,198 --> 00:15:52,368
{\an8}‎You know, it's his birthday this weekend.

251
00:15:54,453 --> 00:15:55,829
{\an8}‎Is it?

252
00:15:55,913 --> 00:15:57,247
{\an8}‎I get it.

253
00:15:57,748 --> 00:15:59,124
{\an8}‎Tough luck, Amamiya.

254
00:15:59,208 --> 00:16:02,211
‎Seeing as it's his birthday,
‎I'm thinking of doing something like this,

255
00:16:02,294 --> 00:16:04,380
‎but I have no sense
‎for these sorts of things.

256
00:16:04,463 --> 00:16:07,132
{\an8}‎Wow. What a great idea!

257
00:16:07,216 --> 00:16:09,885
‎-This'll cheer him right up.
‎-Right?

258
00:16:10,469 --> 00:16:12,721
‎If we're going this route,
‎we should make it funny, yeah?

259
00:16:12,805 --> 00:16:14,682
‎-Right.
‎-What's going on over here?

260
00:16:14,765 --> 00:16:15,766
‎POP
‎A WILD MIDORIKAWA APPEARS!!

261
00:16:17,685 --> 00:16:18,894
‎And so...

262
00:16:19,853 --> 00:16:21,146
‎MINATO AMAMIYA'S SURPRISE
‎BIRTHDAY CELEBRATION PLAN

263
00:16:21,230 --> 00:16:22,815
‎Surprise birthday celebration plan!

264
00:16:23,857 --> 00:16:26,735
‎Let's buy a bunch of things we can use.

265
00:16:26,819 --> 00:16:28,028
‎-Yeah!
‎-Yeah!

266
00:16:28,112 --> 00:16:29,947
‎Shall we get one for Minato?

267
00:16:30,030 --> 00:16:31,490
‎-How's this?
‎-We don't need that.

268
00:16:31,573 --> 00:16:34,034
‎HAHAHA

269
00:16:35,411 --> 00:16:37,538
‎Don't you two have club activities today?

270
00:16:37,621 --> 00:16:41,000
‎Now that the cultural festival's done,
‎we're all just pottering about.

271
00:16:41,083 --> 00:16:44,336
‎And the band club is more just
‎a group of people who do their own thing.

272
00:16:49,216 --> 00:16:50,843
‎Yota says he's done with club activities.

273
00:16:50,926 --> 00:16:51,927
‎Shall I invite him?

274
00:16:54,471 --> 00:16:56,181
<i>‎That was a scare.</i>

275
00:16:56,807 --> 00:17:00,561
<i>‎But hey, it's not like I need to be
‎nervous around him all the time?</i>

276
00:17:01,145 --> 00:17:03,564
<i>‎I mean, he's over it already.</i>

277
00:17:03,647 --> 00:17:05,065
<i>‎It's in the past.</i>

278
00:17:05,149 --> 00:17:08,819
{\an8}<i>‎In fact, it'd be rude
‎to keep making a big deal over it.</i>

279
00:17:12,781 --> 00:17:14,199
‎BAM

280
00:17:14,283 --> 00:17:16,368
<i>‎I think...</i>

281
00:17:16,452 --> 00:17:17,453
‎BA-BUMP BA-BUMP
‎SLURP

282
00:17:17,536 --> 00:17:22,833
{\an8}<i>‎Yota's only ever thinking of ways
‎that he can make you happy.</i>

283
00:17:23,459 --> 00:17:26,462
<i>‎He's not out for you to make him happy.</i>

284
00:17:27,212 --> 00:17:30,257
{\an8}‎To me... You're just Miki.

285
00:17:32,843 --> 00:17:35,345
<i>‎Stop it, stop it! Don't remember that now!</i>

286
00:17:35,429 --> 00:17:37,389
‎You sure can put it away, Yota.

287
00:17:39,850 --> 00:17:41,560
‎Okay, we're headed this way.

288
00:17:43,353 --> 00:17:44,980
‎You are?

289
00:17:45,064 --> 00:17:47,983
‎-Catch ya.
‎-See you tomorrow!

290
00:17:49,777 --> 00:17:52,071
‎Ready to go home?
‎We'll walk together partway.

291
00:17:52,154 --> 00:17:53,655
‎Yeah...

292
00:18:03,082 --> 00:18:05,250
<i>‎Wow, it's just the two of us.</i>

293
00:18:05,334 --> 00:18:06,502
<i>‎Wow... Wow...</i>

294
00:18:07,377 --> 00:18:09,254
<i>‎What do I do?</i>

295
00:18:09,922 --> 00:18:13,133
<i>‎I don't like this.
‎I don't like how this feels.</i>

296
00:18:13,967 --> 00:18:16,470
<i>‎It feels like I'm the one being abnormal.</i>

297
00:18:17,096 --> 00:18:19,014
<i>‎It feels like I can't act natural.</i>

298
00:18:21,350 --> 00:18:23,894
<i>‎I was fine before.</i>

299
00:18:31,068 --> 00:18:33,112
‎-Was that a cat?
‎-Where?

300
00:18:33,195 --> 00:18:35,405
‎I'm sure I just saw an animal.

301
00:18:36,073 --> 00:18:37,449
‎Shall we go look?

302
00:18:37,533 --> 00:18:40,327
‎I wonder what it was?
‎Dang, this is too exciting.

303
00:18:40,410 --> 00:18:42,037
‎What if it's a <i>‎tsuchinoko</i>‎?

304
00:18:44,832 --> 00:18:46,125
‎Look! Over there.

305
00:18:47,292 --> 00:18:49,169
‎STARES...

306
00:18:49,253 --> 00:18:51,672
‎Do you need to go up a prescription level?

307
00:18:51,755 --> 00:18:52,923
‎SNEAKING

308
00:18:53,006 --> 00:18:54,174
‎Ready, and...

309
00:18:54,258 --> 00:18:55,551
‎WHOOSH

310
00:18:55,634 --> 00:18:58,387
‎FLOAT FLOAT

311
00:18:58,470 --> 00:19:00,055
‎*TUMBLEWEED

312
00:19:03,142 --> 00:19:04,143
{\an8}‎What is that?

313
00:19:08,981 --> 00:19:10,691
{\an8}‎No, wait...

314
00:19:10,774 --> 00:19:13,235
‎I could have sworn it was alive.

315
00:19:13,318 --> 00:19:14,444
‎This?

316
00:19:14,528 --> 00:19:15,529
‎FLOAT

317
00:19:17,781 --> 00:19:19,199
‎What even is this?

318
00:19:19,283 --> 00:19:20,576
‎Don't ask me!

319
00:19:20,659 --> 00:19:23,203
<i>‎I thought these only appeared in Westerns.</i>

320
00:19:24,163 --> 00:19:25,164
‎THERE THERE

321
00:19:25,247 --> 00:19:27,583
‎I think I'm getting attached.
‎There there, little guy.

322
00:19:36,049 --> 00:19:37,593
<i>‎I knew it.</i>

323
00:19:39,428 --> 00:19:41,305
<i>‎I do like spending time with Yota.</i>

324
00:19:43,557 --> 00:19:45,726
<i>‎I like who I am when I'm with him.</i>

325
00:19:47,728 --> 00:19:49,271
<i>‎I like Yota.</i>

326
00:19:51,356 --> 00:19:53,692
<i>‎And not just as a partner or a friend.</i>

327
00:19:54,359 --> 00:19:55,819
<i>‎I like him for "him."</i>

328
00:19:57,404 --> 00:19:59,281
<i>‎It's so simple.</i>

329
00:20:00,073 --> 00:20:02,367
<i>‎This is how it was always meant to be.</i>

330
00:20:02,993 --> 00:20:06,705
<i>‎So why am I always
‎overthinking things now?</i>

331
00:20:08,457 --> 00:20:10,792
‎Well, that was good for a laugh.

332
00:20:10,876 --> 00:20:11,877
‎Ready to head back?

333
00:20:13,587 --> 00:20:15,130
‎Bye-bye, Pokojiro.

334
00:20:15,214 --> 00:20:16,381
‎Pokota's little brother?

335
00:20:18,717 --> 00:20:20,552
‎Heave-ho, heave-ho...

336
00:20:20,636 --> 00:20:22,304
‎Wow, it's a lot harder going back up.

337
00:20:22,387 --> 00:20:23,388
‎Yeah.

338
00:20:27,935 --> 00:20:28,936
‎Got you.

339
00:20:30,938 --> 00:20:33,106
‎Are you all right? Take care now.

340
00:20:33,190 --> 00:20:34,358
‎Yeah...

341
00:20:34,983 --> 00:20:36,360
‎Thanks.

342
00:20:41,865 --> 00:20:42,866
‎Ready, and...

343
00:20:42,950 --> 00:20:44,368
‎Hup!

344
00:20:45,869 --> 00:20:47,454
‎I was not prepared.

345
00:20:47,537 --> 00:20:48,997
‎Keep it together.

346
00:20:49,581 --> 00:20:52,000
<i>‎Don't overthink it. Don't overthink it.</i>

347
00:20:52,084 --> 00:20:53,752
<i>‎Simple. Keep it simple.</i>

348
00:21:00,842 --> 00:21:02,511
{\an8}<i>‎-That breeze--</i>
‎-Hey.

349
00:21:03,178 --> 00:21:04,596
‎I love this breeze.

350
00:21:07,224 --> 00:21:08,558
‎Autumn's on the way.

351
00:21:09,768 --> 00:21:11,353
‎It's kind of exciting, huh?

352
00:21:11,895 --> 00:21:13,063
‎But moments like these,

353
00:21:13,146 --> 00:21:16,441
‎when it gets cool
‎and you feel the seasonal change,

354
00:21:16,525 --> 00:21:18,777
‎these are the moments
‎that get me the most excited.

355
00:21:21,613 --> 00:21:22,614
<i>‎Uh-oh...</i>

356
00:21:24,491 --> 00:21:26,994
<i>‎There's no denying it now.</i>

357
00:21:27,995 --> 00:21:31,790
<i>‎Wait, no way... What?</i>

358
00:21:31,873 --> 00:21:34,126
<i>‎No. It can't be...</i>

359
00:21:36,420 --> 00:21:38,088
‎See you tomorrow.

360
00:22:00,068 --> 00:22:03,405
<i>‎I'm still smiling from all the fun we had.</i>

361
00:22:04,948 --> 00:22:10,746
<i>‎I feel light on my feet, floaty,
‎from excitement and nerves.</i>

362
00:22:11,705 --> 00:22:14,374
<i>‎And yet my heart feels clogged.</i>

363
00:22:14,958 --> 00:22:16,251
<i>‎Like I'm about to cry.</i>

364
00:22:16,960 --> 00:22:19,421
<i>‎What do I do?</i>

365
00:22:20,422 --> 00:22:22,883
<i>‎This is love, plain and simple.</i>

366
00:23:50,929 --> 00:23:55,934
{\an8}‎Subtitle translation by: Rychelle Brittain

